  "captions": [
    {"start": 0.401, "end": 4.561, "lines": ["Yeah, broadly, if there's a mission going","on at NASA that involves humans,"]},
    {"start": 4.561, "end": 7.041, "lines": ["HRP is generally involved."]},
    {"start": 7.041, "end": 9.983, "lines": ["And that's because we're trying","to understand how."]},
    {"start": 10.128, "end": 14.288, "lines": ["All of the different ways","that we fly affect the human."]},
    {"start": 14.288, "end": 17.728, "lines": ["Short flights, you know,","we were doing shuttle data"]},
    {"start": 17.728, "end": 19.728, "lines": ["for a while, very short flights."]},
    {"start": 19.728, "end": 24.048, "lines": ["Even Artemis II, it was a short flight,","but it's a very new flight environment."]},
    {"start": 24.048, "end": 27.328, "lines": ["It's a new mission cadence that we need"]},
    {"start": 27.328, "end": 30.208, "lines": ["to understand and be prepared for.","And then, of course,"]},
    {"start": 30.208, "end": 32.688, "lines": ["ISS, which is kind","of established at this point,"]},
    {"start": 32.688, "end": 36.848, "lines": ["but we're still learning new things about","how the human body reacts to spaceflight"]},
    {"start": 36.848, "end": 40.112, "lines": ["or microgravity","on a long-duration mission."]},
    {"start": 40.112, "end": 41.792, "lines": ["Like a Mars mission."]},
    {"start": 41.792, "end": 47.072, "lines": ["So, that combined with what we learned","in ground analogs about how it feels"]},
    {"start": 47.072, "end": 50.912, "lines": ["to live in an isolated and confined","environment for a very long period"]},
    {"start": 50.912, "end": 55.352, "lines": ["of time, help us better prepare","for these upcoming missions that are."]},
    {"start": 55.744, "end": 58.064, "lines": ["Our challenges that we've never done","before."]},
    {"start": 58.064, "end": 60.864, "lines": ["So, there's a lot that we can learn","from CHAPEA,"]},
    {"start": 60.864, "end": 63.384, "lines": ["and I think that's the value of it:"]},
    {"start": 63.824, "end": 68.544, "lines": ["it can be very broad in what we can learn.","There's lots of things we can learn"]},
    {"start": 68.544, "end": 71.984, "lines": ["specific to behavioral health","and performance, but there's also lots"]},
    {"start": 71.984, "end": 76.144, "lines": ["of things we're learning","about what we need in a food system"]},
    {"start": 76.144, "end": 82.184, "lines": ["for exploration, what we need","from exercise, how EVAs might work."]},
    {"start": 82.48, "end": 84.08, "lines": ["Like surface EVAs going"]},
    {"start": 84.08, "end": 87.76, "lines": ["out to do a Mars walk is probably","a very different experience"]},
    {"start": 87.76, "end": 91.68, "lines": ["and a very different coordination","with the ground here on Earth"]},
    {"start": 91.68, "end": 96.64, "lines": ["than it would be in our traditional","EVAs that you see on ISS."]},
    {"start": 96.64, "end": 102.64, "lines": ["Those are very well coordinated","and orchestrated by MCC on the ground,"]},
    {"start": 102.64, "end": 106.736, "lines": ["whereas on Mars, because of our delay,","we're not going to see that."]},
    {"start": 106.736, "end": 111.616, "lines": ["In our last episode, we took a deep dive","into spacewalks or Mars walks,"]},
    {"start": 111.616, "end": 116.816, "lines": ["and we got an update on this audio log","about how many they have been supporting,"]},
    {"start": 116.816, "end": 118.976, "lines": ["which I was surprised to hear."]},
    {"start": 118.976, "end": 122.496, "lines": ["And talking about the future,","what are you looking most forward"]},
    {"start": 122.496, "end": 126.144, "lines": ["to when it comes to the future","of analog studies here at NASA?"]},
    {"start": 126.576, "end": 129.896, "lines": ["I'm super excited about analogs,","because I think it's…"]},
    {"start": 130.976, "end": 132.8, "lines": ["our creative outlet."]},
    {"start": 132.8, "end": 138.24, "lines": ["It's our opportunity","to explore what future sustaining lunar"]},
    {"start": 138.24, "end": 141.12, "lines": ["or Mars missions might look like."]},
    {"start": 141.12, "end": 145.28, "lines": ["Learn some of these really critical","areas that we're not necessarily"]},
    {"start": 145.28, "end": 146.96, "lines": ["thinking about right now."]},
    {"start": 146.96, "end": 148.76, "lines": ["These changes in operational"]},
    {"start": 149.184, "end": 150.504, "lines": ["designs"]},
    {"start": 150.944, "end": 154.784, "lines": ["or how we run our MCC, for example."]},
    {"start": 154.784, "end": 158.624, "lines": ["These are all opportunities where","we can get creative as an agency and say,"]},
    {"start": 158.624, "end": 161.344, "lines": ["how do we think we need","to do this differently?"]},
    {"start": 161.344, "end": 163.584, "lines": ["What do we need to look for?"]},
    {"start": 163.584, "end": 165.544, "lines": ["What have we not even thought of?"]},
    {"start": 166.048, "end": 169.648, "lines": ["And analogs is our best way of doing that."]},
    {"start": 169.648, "end": 172.928, "lines": ["It's both cheaper","to do it on the ground first,"]},
    {"start": 172.928, "end": 177.328, "lines": ["but also it's faster that we can change","over our science."]},
    {"start": 177.328, "end": 181.488, "lines": ["We can iterate our science faster","on the ground than we can by flying"]},
    {"start": 181.488, "end": 182.528, "lines": ["our science."]},
    {"start": 182.528, "end": 186.608, "lines": ["So that's why ground analogs","is actually a really critical component"]},
    {"start": 186.608, "end": 192.088, "lines": ["of human health research beyond just","what we learn from our flight crews."]},
    {"start": 192.72, "end": 195.84, "lines": ["Sarah, thank you for coming","on Houston Weave a podcast today."]},
    {"start": 195.84, "end": 197.723, "lines": ["Thank you so much for having me."]},
    {"start": 198.16, "end": 200.72, "lines": ["Now let's hear from Ross,","Ellen, Matthew and James"]},
    {"start": 200.72, "end": 204.8, "lines": ["as they unpack what life is like just","after Mars Dune Alpha regained signal"]},
